  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessment Dairy Training Center of Excellence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India has been the world&apos;s largest dairy producer for two decades. However, milk yield per cow remains low, compared to other countries, and ensuring stable milk quality, efficient collection and adequate cooling remains a challenge. The Indian government aims to produce 30% of the world&#x2019;s milk by 2030 for both domestic consumption and export. But doing so by primarily increasing herd sizes will have severe environmental consequences, including higher greenhouse gas emissions, water use, feed waste and antibiotic overuse. To address these challenges, the Indian Ministry of Animal Husbandry, Dairying and Fisheries desires to establish a Dairy Training Center of Excellence in Bangalore, which shall play a crucial role in modernising the dairy sector in Southern India. By providing practical training and fostering sustainable practices, the Centre will help increase productivity, improve livelihoods and farmers&#x2019; income and contribute to the overall development of the dairy industry. The purpose of this project is to conduct a needs assessment and formulate boundary conditions and criteria necessary for the establishment of a sustainable, innovative and demand driven Dairy Training Center of Excellence near Bangalore, India.</narrative>
  </description>
